- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SetupGridPanelTests`

**How to implement.** The grid generator's panel, a surface in a file of its own, opened from the slot bar and shown between it and the table (001 §O 'Slot bar over the table (§J), with "Record experiment"; the grid generator' and 'Automation': `SetupGridGenerateButton`; 001 §J 'Grid generator'; the S8.4 brief: 'The grid-generator UI (SetupGridGenerateButton) runs over S8.3'; .spec-md §4 'UI', §10.5). Like the slot bar (step 280) it is compiled before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` as a projection of its own state and handler records. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: in the slot-bar group (step 280), `setupGridOpenButton` (`"SetupGridOpenButton"`); and a new group after it, `// --- The setup grid generator (SetupGridView). ---`: `setupGridPanel` (`"SetupGridPanel"`), `setupGridCombinationList` (`"SetupGridCombinationList"`), `setupGridGenerateButton` (`"SetupGridGenerateButton"`, 001 §O's id), `setupGridCloseButton` (`"SetupGridCloseButton"`) and `static member setupGridCombination (position : ConstructorUiPosition) : ConstructorUiId` (`SetupGridCombination_<n>`, over `UiIds.fs:ConstructorUiPosition`), each with a one-line doc. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each with a one-line doc: on the `ConstructorUiId` extension, `static member setupGridItemChoice (role : Setups.SlotRole) (item : Kit.ItemId) : ConstructorUiId` (`SetupGridItem_<role.uiKey>_<the item's GUID>`), `static member setupGridAngleField (role : Setups.SlotRole) : ConstructorUiId` (`SetupGridAngleField_<role.uiKey>`) and `static member setupGridAngle (role : Setups.SlotRole) (angle : Angle) : ConstructorUiId` (`SetupGridAngle_<role.uiKey>_<the angle's degrees as degreeCaption writes them, without the °>`); and `type SetupGrids.GridCombination with member this.caption (table : Setups.SetupSlot list) (items : Kit.Item list) : ControlCaption`: each pick, in order, as `<the role.text of its slot in the table's light order>: <the item's label> @ <r1.degreeCaption>` (`—` for nothing, `(not in this kit)` for an item `items` lacks), joined by `, `, and `The table as it is` for a combination of no pick. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SetupGridView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.SetupGridView`, compiled directly after `SlotBarView.fs` and before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment, and a module doc of one to three lines. It declares, each with a one-line doc: `GridCombinationMark` = `CombinationTicked` | `CombinationUnticked` | `CombinationImpossible of reason : ControlCaption`, never stored, so with no wire tag; `GridCombinationState = { combination : SetupGrids.GridCombination; caption : ControlCaption; mark : GridCombinationMark }`; `SetupGridSlotState = { roled : Setups.RoledSlot; fitting : Kit.Item list; draft : SetupGrids.GridSlotDraft }`; `SetupGridState = { grid : SetupGrids.SetupGrid; slots : SetupGridSlotState list; rows : GridCombinationState list; generateAvailability : ControlAvailability }`; and `SetupGridHandlers = { toggleItem : Library.ElementId -> Kit.ItemId -> unit; addAngle : Library.ElementId -> RotationControls.BarDegrees -> unit; removeAngle : Library.ElementId -> Angle -> unit; toggleCombination : SetupGrids.GridCombination -> unit; generateGrid : SetupGrids.SetupGrid -> unit; closeGrid : unit -> unit }`; and `setupGridView (state : SetupGridState) (handlers : SetupGridHandlers) : IView`. The view is a `Border` carrying `setupGridPanel`, margin 8, 0, 8, 4, over a vertical `StackPanel` holding: (a) the semi-bold `Setup grid` and the wrapping line `Choose the items and the R1 angles to try in each slot. Every ticked combination becomes a setup of the kit, with an experiment of the draft over each.`; (b) for each of `slots`, a `DockPanel` whose left is `<role.text>:` and whose fill is a `WrapPanel` holding each `fitting` item as a box carrying `setupGridItemChoice role item.id` with `item.label.caption`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` while the draft holds the item and a `verbButton` otherwise, either calling `toggleItem`; then `R1 (°):` and a `TextBox` carrying `setupGridAngleField role`, width 60, whose text on Enter or losing focus is read by `BarDegrees.tryCreate` (`RotationControls.fs:60`) and, when it reads, passed to `addAngle` and the field cleared, an unreadable text being left as typed and ignored (the rotation bar's field rule, `RotationControls.fs:236`); then each of the draft's angles as a box carrying `setupGridAngle role angle` reading `<angle.degreeCaption> ×` and calling `removeAngle`; (c) `Combinations:` over a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `setupGridCombinationList`, one line per `rows` entry in order carrying `setupGridCombination` of its 1-based position: a ticked one a box reading `☑ <caption>`, an unticked one `☐ <caption>`, either calling `toggleCombination` (the element menu's marks, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3733`), and an impossible one a `TextBlock` reading `✗ <caption> — <reason>` in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`, which takes no press; (d) one horizontal `StackPanel` of `Generate` (`setupGridGenerateButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` calling `generateGrid grid`, present only when `generateAvailability` is `ControlOffered`) and `Close` (`setupGridCloseButton`, on `negativeBackground`, calling `closeGrid`), the action box's right margin being the gap (.spec-md §10.5). Every id is an AutomationId. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs` (step 280): `SlotBarHandlers` gains `openSetupGrid : unit -> unit`, and the chip row ends, after `Record experiment`, with the verb `Setup grid…` (`setupGridOpenButton`) calling it; the grid's edits write nothing, so it is offered under a read-only kit too. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: on the model extension holding `setupGrid` (step 282), `member model.setupGridState : SetupGridView.SetupGridState option`, `None` while `setupGrid` is: its `slots` one per `SetupSlot.inLightOrder model.elements` with `model.slotChipItems slot` and the draft's `slotDraft slot.id`; its `rows` one per `grid.combinations`, captioned by `caption model.elements model.kitItems` and marked `CombinationImpossible` with the `describe` of `combination.slotsOver model.elements model.kitItems model.tryItemModelChoice`'s error (step 274), else `CombinationTicked` when `grid.ticked` holds it and `CombinationUnticked` otherwise; and `generateAvailability` `ControlOffered` when `model.kitWrites` is (step 185), the grid has an axis and `ticked` is not empty, and `ControlWithheld` otherwise. A private `setupGridHandlers (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : SetupGridView.SetupGridHandlers` beside `slotBarHandlers` dispatches `ToggleSetupGridItem`, `AddSetupGridAngle`, `RemoveSetupGridAngle`, `ToggleSetupGridCombination`, `GenerateSetupGrid` (step 276) and `CloseSetupGrid`, and `slotBarHandlers` gains `openSetupGrid` dispatching `OpenSetupGrid`. The table surface's `DockPanel` (step 280) docks, below the slot bar and above the table, `SetupGridView.setupGridView state (setupGridHandlers dispatch)` while `setupGridState` is `Some state`. No other message, field, id or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SetupGridPanelTests.fs`, `module SetupGridPanelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, mounting `mainView` as `SlotBarTests` does (step 280), over `initMain ()` whose scratch kit holds `LP1`, `LP2`, `QZ` and `QZ2` added through the Items panel's messages, with a linear polarizer, a sample and a second linear polarizer added so that the light meets them in that order before the seeded detector, `LP1` in the first and `LP2` in the second (`AssignSlot`). Without a trait: `the setup grid UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the five fixed ids' texts, `setupGridCombination (ConstructorUiPosition 2)` (`SetupGridCombination_2`), `setupGridItemChoice (ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))` of a test-local item id (`SetupGridItem_Obj1_<its GUID>`), `setupGridAngleField (AnalyzerSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))` (`SetupGridAngleField_Analyzer1`) and `setupGridAngle (ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)) (Angle.degree 22.5)` (`SetupGridAngle_Obj1_22.5`). `the grid panel sits between the slot bar and the table, offers each slot's fitting items and angles, and marks each combination ticked, unticked or impossible`: after `OpenSetupGrid`, `setupGridPanel`'s top is below the bar's bottom and its bottom above the canvas's top, with a row for Source, Prep 1, Obj 1, Analyzer 1 and Detector 1, Obj 1's offering `QZ` and `QZ2` and Prep 1's `LP1` and `LP2`; after `ToggleSetupGridItem` of the sample with `QZ` and `QZ2`, `AddSetupGridAngle` of 0° and 45° and `ToggleSetupGridCombination` of (`QZ2`, 45°), `setupGridCombinationList` reads, in order, `☑ Obj 1: QZ @ 0°`, `☑ Obj 1: QZ @ 45°`, `☑ Obj 1: QZ2 @ 0°` and `☐ Obj 1: QZ2 @ 45°`; and with Prep 1 trying `LP1` and `LP2` and Analyzer 1 trying `LP2`, each combination putting `LP2` in both is a line starting `✗ ` and ending `the item is in two slots: ` and the reason naming `LP2` (`SlotItemTwiceErr`, step 274). `Generate and Close share a row, Close to the right, and Generate needs a ticked combination over a slot`: with the panel open and no axis, `setupGridGenerateButton` is absent and `setupGridCloseButton` present; with an item tried, `Generate` and `Close` have equal tops, `Close`'s left beyond `Generate`'s right; and pressing `setupGridCloseButton` removes the panel. `a kit opened read-only offers the grid but no Generate`: with the model's kit replaced, by record update, by the read-only view of its scratch kit (step 131), as `ItemsPanelTests`' read-only fact builds its model (step 241), and the grid open with `QZ` tried in the sample, `setupGridOpenButton` and `setupGridPanel` are present and `setupGridGenerateButton` absent. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing boxes at their centre as `LibraryWindowTests